'''Dhungaloo''' (Dungaloo) is an extinct<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Glottolog 5.2 - Gureng Gureng |url=https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/gure1255 |access-date=2025-12-10 |website=glottolog.org}}</ref> [[Australian Aboriginal language]] of [[Queensland]]. Bowern<ref>Bowern, Claire. 2011. "[http://anggarrgoon.wordpress.com/2011/12/23/how-many-languages-were-spoken-in-australia/ How Many Languages Were Spoken in Australia?]", ''Anggarrgoon: Australian languages on the web'', 23 December 2011 ([http://pamanyungan.sites.yale.edu/master-list-australian-languages-v12 corrected] 6 February 2012)</ref> suggests that it may have been a [[Maric languages|Maric language]]. However, AIATSIS has no listing for the name, listing a Dungaloo wordlist under [[Taribelang language|Taribelang]] (Gureng-Gureng).<ref>{{Cite web |title=Collections {{!}} AIATSIS corporate website |url=https://aiatsis.gov.au/collections/item/M0069305 |access-date=2025-12-10 |website=aiatsis.gov.au}}</ref><ref name=AIATSIS/> Glottolog does the same, treating it as a dialect of Gureng Gureng.<ref name=":0" />

